WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.264 --> 00:00:02.847
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:10.978
- [Announcer] And Rodgers
is gonna begin to take off

00:00:10.978 --> 00:00:13.337
and then fire, and it's caught, touchdown.

00:00:13.337 --> 00:00:17.173
- [Announcer] He's in the block,
Rodgers throws another one.

00:00:17.173 --> 00:00:18.110
(upbeat music)

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:21.420
- 2005 Draft Night we have our
board, it's up on the wall.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.330
If people see me on the board,

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.420
you know, see me showing the board here.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:28.460
So first round grades, this is every team.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.810
- Yeah, everybody grades everybody.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:32.100
- At that time we had maybe 20 players

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.700
above a first round line, okay.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.600
We didn't have 32, we had 20.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.640
- 20 people you think were
worth the first round pick.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:39.710
- Worth the first round pick.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.830
24 was our pick, 24.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:44.620
So two things happened that night.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:49.620
Number one, everyone we wanted
except one player got taken.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.090
We wanted DeMarcus Ware bad, Dallas.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:57.290
We wanted Marcus Spears bad, Dallas.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:02.213
We wanted the guy on ESPN, my
friend, Pollack, Cincinnati.

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.304
We wanted Derrick Johnson, Kansas City.

00:01:06.304 --> 00:01:09.760
We wanted Pacman, Tennessee.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.450
So the second thing that happened,

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:15.120
yeah there were issues there.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:18.040
The second thing that
happened was no one was takin'

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.760
the quarterback Aaron Rodgers.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:23.440
Now, Gruden had told him he's
gonna take him to his face,

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:26.230
Gruden takes Cadillac Williams.

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:27.900
Tennessee we thought, they're taking him,

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:28.840
no, they took Pacman.

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:32.040
Kansas City we thought, no
they took Derrick Johnson.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.870
We're comin' up on this and now Gary,

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.630
you gotta picture this.

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:39.340
I'm in the middle, we got
management, Ted on the left

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:43.380
with Mike, I'm sorry,
Mike Sherman not McCarthy,

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:46.390
is over here and all these
offensive coaches and stuff

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:47.360
are over here.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.860
We're about to sort
of, get up to our spot,

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:52.970
and these offensive coaches are yanking,

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:55.370
and they're like, Andrew we can't do this.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:56.710
We cannot do this.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:57.543
- 'Cause we don't need him.

00:01:57.543 --> 00:02:00.483
We got Favre in place,
we've got other needs.

00:02:00.483 --> 00:02:01.720
And who do they want?

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:02.960
- The last thing you want as a coach

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.590
is taking a player in the first round

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.850
that will not help you.

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.370
Not help you this year,
not help you next year,

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:09.960
maybe not help you ever.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.900
So they want us to dip into
our second round grades

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.750
and take offensive line.
- Offensive line, a receiver.

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.150
- Or even the defensive coaches.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:19.290
- [Man] Had he been on the board at all?

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:20.190
- Yeah, he's a first round grade.

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:23.380
- He's our only player up
there in the first round grade.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:25.924
- They just never thought
they'd ever get him.

00:02:25.924 --> 00:02:29.620
Andy, it was 50/50 that he was
gonna go number one overall.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:32.820
Alex Smith went one, and then
the whole dominoes happen.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:35.030
- So now we've got all the management...

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:36.210
- Andrew real quick, real quick,

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.590
'cause I like breaking up
the stories real quick.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.640
Gut feeling, do you think Aaron Rodgers

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.340
has as successful a career
if he goes one over all?

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.120
- [Andrew] No.
- [Gary] You don't.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:49.620
You do believe, like you knew,

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.030
you would think he would be good,

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:53.830
but you do believe that
something happened in that hour,

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:57.040
a couple hours, that chip on the shoulder

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.960
was a tremendous fuel for more success?

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.970
- Yeah, and I think
backing up Brett helped.

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:04.140
He hated it, but I think it helped,

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:05.650
rather than being thrown into whatever

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:07.073
was going on in San Francisco.

00:03:07.073 --> 00:03:08.630
- So that's not what I'm asking,

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:09.463
'cause that's a different question,

00:03:09.463 --> 00:03:10.480
which is a great question.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:13.440
Which is sitting behind Favre
for three years, did it help?

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.830
Separate question, chip on shoulder.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:18.150
- Yeah, I think so 'cause
he played that well.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:21.410
He trades on that and he's
good at trading on that.

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:23.480
- Brady does it too, I do it too.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.350
I'm an immigrant, I got Ds and Fs.

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:28.100
- I always told Aaron,
Brady's 200 you're 24.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.360
I mean, how many players want to be 24?

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.040
- He's like fuck you Andrew,
I should've been one.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.380
Fuck Alex Smith, that's what he says.

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:37.520
- Finishing up that story, they
say, what do we always say.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:39.310
Now these GMs are now all GMs,

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:40.310
Reggie McKenzie, John Schneider.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:41.510
- Take the best player on the board.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:44.150
- Right.
- Doesn't matter.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:45.230
If the Jets' do that this year,

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:47.610
we don't need more defense
Jets, if you're listening.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:48.443
Go ahead.

00:03:48.443 --> 00:03:49.465
- Trust the board.

00:03:49.465 --> 00:03:53.237
So here's the story, Ted Thompson says,

00:03:53.237 --> 00:03:54.070
"Get him on the phone."

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:56.100
I thought he meant him,
meaning the agent Mike Sullivan

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.630
who I've known forever.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:01.230
I call the number, "Hello."

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:02.063
Mike?

00:04:02.063 --> 00:04:03.320
Mike's the agent's name.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.160
No, it's Aaron.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.260
Oh my gosh.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.010
Aaron it's Andrew Brandt
from the Green Bay Packers.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:08.630
Can I talk to Mike?

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:11.410
And I felt so bad, and
then Aaron's, you know,

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:12.560
Mike's like, are you gonna take him,

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:13.393
are you gonna take him, you take him?

00:04:13.393 --> 00:04:14.226
I'm like, hold on.

00:04:14.226 --> 00:04:16.840
So my instructions are,
fifteen minutes then,

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:17.880
and Aaron's in this room.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.420
The caterer's have packed up everything,

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:21.743
he's been there five hours, the parents.

00:04:24.929 --> 00:04:26.890
- [Gary] He's supposed to go one, it's 23,

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:27.980
the camera's in his face all the time.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:28.923
- [Andrew] They changed
the rule after that year.

00:04:28.923 --> 00:04:31.770
- That's right, in his
face the whole time,

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.030
and he's getting more pissed.

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:34.390
The whole world's watching

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:35.470
and you're just slippin' and slippin'.

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:37.690
- So I've gotta keep him
there 12 more minutes.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:38.977
I said, "Keep him on the phone 12 minutes,

00:04:38.977 --> 00:04:41.720
"and let's see if that phone rings."

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:43.260
- Because you guys had decided

00:04:44.474 --> 00:04:46.330
that if somebody called you...

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:49.453
- Not any offer, but
if we got a good offer,

00:04:50.663 --> 00:04:55.060
a decent offer, the whole
NFL would look different.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:59.520
That phone, 12 minutes,
I'm watching Aaron,

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:00.777
I'm watching Mike talk to me on the phone.

00:05:00.777 --> 00:05:02.460
- And guys real quick, for everybody's

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:05.150
who's not a football nerd, at 24,

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:06.930
all those teams in the first round,

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:08.470
that were heavily considering him

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:10.760
but for some reason went elsewhere,

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:13.290
it wouldn't have cost them a fortune,

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:15.070
they could've used a second round pick

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:16.890
and some other collateral,
it wouldn't have been...

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:17.723
- I don't know.

00:05:17.723 --> 00:05:20.030
Maybe second and third, maybe two twos.

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:22.370
- Two twos, or a second and a third,

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:24.300
to move back into the first round,

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:26.720
take who they wanted at nine, Pacman,

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:27.610
Tennessee coulda had him.

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:28.443
I mean, they had McNair.

00:05:28.443 --> 00:05:30.040
I'm trying to remember,
it's hard to remember,

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:33.240
but it wasn't like you had the fourth pick

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:35.080
where it's like you're
giving up two drafts

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:36.260
to get one guy.

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:41.230
It wasn't hard to go into 24
from the early second round,

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:42.910
have your cake and eat it too,

00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:45.760
and take Aaron Fuckin'
Rodgers, but nobody called.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:46.620
- Crickets, crickets.

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.260
- And you guys said, fuck
it, we'll just take him.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:51.190
- Two minutes left on the
clock, Ted says tell him.

00:05:51.190 --> 00:05:53.350
I tell him and we...

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:54.370
- You're like on the phone with him

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:55.203
bullshitting for 10 minutes.

00:05:55.203 --> 00:05:57.300
- Yeah, and I'm not saying a word.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:59.410
I'm not saying a word
'cause I don't want it,

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:00.370
I don't want to hear it.

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:01.860
I'm like Mike, you just gotta hold,

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:03.450
you gotta stay with me here.

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:05.410
Longest 12 minutes of
Aaron's life, I'm sure.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:06.243
- And then what?

00:06:06.243 --> 00:06:08.493
You say, Aaron congratulations
you're a Green Bay Packer?

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:14.310
- With the 24th selection
in the 2005 NFL Draft,

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:17.080
the Green Bay Packers
select Aaron Rodgers,

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.660
quarterback from California.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:20.970
- I immediately get a
call from Favre, agent.

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:22.660
- Immediately?
- Immediately.

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:26.170
Favre talked to the coach.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:28.020
- Who was that, Bus Cook?
- Bus Cook.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:30.660
And then we have a draft party.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.500
Listen to this, we have
a draft party going on

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:36.707
in Lambeau, I don't know,
1,000 people, right below us.

00:06:36.707 --> 00:06:37.990
"Boo!"

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:40.260
Oh my God were they booing.

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:42.023
And I'm like, come on guys.

00:06:43.068 --> 00:06:44.950
- What was Bus saying,
yelling his ass off?

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:46.050
- He's like, "What the fuck's going on?"

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:47.500
- Yeah, why are you doing that?

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.920
- Like, what are you
doing, replacement, what?

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:52.910
I'm like, just hold on, just hold on.

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:55.343
And I had that conversation
over three years.

00:06:57.190 --> 00:06:59.300
- You had two parties and
you were in the middle.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:02.450
- Like for three years, Bus
at Brett's side is like,

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:05.210
are you just trying to replace us, no.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:08.880
Aaron's side is, he's never gonna play.

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:10.130
What are you doing?
- [Gary] Trade us.

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:12.090
Did they ever really push for trade?

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:14.820
- No, not in those terms.

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:15.760
- [Gary] They alluded to it?

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:20.760
- I heard the phrase, he's
never gonna retire, many times.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:24.030
- They were right, he kinda didn't.

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:26.520
- Well, I mean for years we
asked Brett to come back,

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:28.560
and that last year we frankly, didn't.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.040
We didn't say, don't come back,

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.140
but we said, it's up to you.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:33.880
- Yeah, he didn't like
the way you phrased it.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:34.773
- I guess.

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:38.850
Now he retired, a big,
teary press conference.

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:42.770
In hindsight, in hindsight, Mark Murphy

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:45.833
or someone should've had
the conversation which is,

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:49.070
we think you might want to
come back at some point.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:51.870
You might get that itch
and we're letting you know,

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:53.510
we're turning the keys over here.

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:56.330
Because when he did come
back I was in that room.

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.130
I heard that conversation where

00:07:58.130 --> 00:08:00.890
Mike McCarthy said those three words.

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:01.906
We've moved on.

00:08:01.906 --> 00:08:04.489
(upbeat music)

00:08:07.992 --> 00:08:10.377
- [Announcer] Rodgers
dancing, fires down field,

00:08:10.377 --> 00:08:15.224
(mumbling) he's got it, touchdown.

00:08:15.224 --> 00:08:17.574
- [Announcer] Wait,
Rodgers gets up, floats it,

00:08:19.101 --> 00:08:20.434
Cobb, touchdown.

00:08:22.392 --> 00:08:24.130
- [Announcer] You reset Starks.

00:08:24.130 --> 00:08:25.940
They are gonna bring pressure again.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:29.480
Rodgers is gonna roll away,
throws it up in the air,

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:31.880
says a prayer, and (mumbling), please,

00:08:35.667 --> 00:08:38.143
what a catch, that's insane.

00:08:38.143 --> 00:08:40.726
(upbeat music)

